==German==
[[File:Buletten.jpg|thumb|Frikadellen]]

===Etymology===
From early modern {{etyl|nl|de}} {{m|nl|frikadel}}, which is borrowed from {{etyl|fr|de}} {{m|fr|fricadel}}, an only later attested variant of {{m|fr|fricandeau}}. A further relation with {{cog|it|frittatella|}} is speculative. Compare contemporary {{cog|nl|frikandel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌfʁɪkaˈdɛlə/|/ˌfʁiːka-/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Frikadellen}}

# {{lb|de|regional}} {{l|en|meatball}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Frikadelle'' is the most widely accepted word for “meatball” in German. It is nevertheless regionally bound and heard most often in central-western and north-western Germany.

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-f|n}}

